sentences.l:
and heard his lady mother,
sitting in the depths of the sea beside her old father,
and cried out then;

Him I, having reared him like a plant on the rich ground of an orchard,
sent forth upon the curved ships into Ilium
to fight the Trojans;

and they, with her,
tearful went, and around them the wave of the sea
was breaking;

sentences.t:
ἀλλὰ τί μοι τῶν ἦδος ἐπεὶ φίλος ὤλεθ’ ἑταῖρος
Πάτροκλος, τὸν ἐγὼ περὶ πάντων τῖον ἑταίρων
ἶσον ἐμῇ κεφαλῇ;

sentences.tr:
alla ti moi tōn ēdos epei philos ōleth’ hetairos
Patroklos, ton egō peri pantōn tion hetairōn
ison emēi kephalēi;

sentences.l:
I lost him, and the armour Hector,
having cut him down, stripped off, huge, a wonder to behold,
fine;
